::Q01::Which Python file mode should you use when you need to add new data to an existing file while preserving its current contents?{
~w
=a
~r+
~w+
}

::Q02::What is the main advantage of using `with open(...)` when working with a file?{
~It creates a new file if the file does not exist
~It automatically changes the file mode after reading
~It automatically appends new data to the file
=It automatically closes the file when the code block is finished
}

::Q03::What happens when an existing file containing data is opened using mode `w`?{
~The existing data is preserved and new data is added to the end
~The file is opened only for reading
~An error is always raised
=The existing data is overwritten (truncated)
}

::Q04::Which statement correctly describes Python file mode `r+`?{
~It only appends data and cannot read the file
~It allows reading and writing but always creates a new file
~It only reads the file and creates it if it does not exist
=It allows both reading and writing, starts at the beginning, and requires the file to exist
}

::Q05::In the filename "myproject.docx", what does ".docx" represent?{
=The file extension
~The file path
~The file mode
~The directory name
}
